WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.310 --> 00:00:04.730
Despite the fact that it covers the majority
of our planet’s surface, we know remarkably

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:06.509
little about the oceans.

00:00:06.509 --> 00:00:10.620
Well, we know how to navigate them and how
to send boats from one continent to another

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:16.240
- the surface of the water is usually a calm,
safe place where all you expect to encounter

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.920
are other humans and the occasional storm.

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.869
What’s below the surface is another story.

00:00:22.869 --> 00:00:26.910
Scientists estimate that we’ve only explored
maybe 5 percent of the world’s oceans and

00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:28.699
what lies in them.

00:00:28.699 --> 00:00:33.230
On top of that, they estimate that we’ve
only encountered and cataloged 10 percent

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:34.770
of marine life.

00:00:34.770 --> 00:00:40.680
That means that 95 percent of the ocean is
unexplored and untouched by humans, and that

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:44.790
90 percent of the ocean species have never
even been seen by humans.

00:00:44.790 --> 00:00:48.690
It makes you think - just what kind of stuff
is down there?

00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:50.250
It could be anything.

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:53.990
Even mundane ocean life can be deeply strange
and bizarre.

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:59.100
There are sharks that live for over three
hundred years, blind fish that hunt by only

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:02.690
smell, jellyfish that are ‘reborn’ whenever
they die.

00:01:02.690 --> 00:01:08.170
If normal ocean life is this terrifying and
explanation-defying, what kinds of anomalies

00:01:08.170 --> 00:01:12.170
could the oceans we swim and fish in be playing
host to?

00:01:12.170 --> 00:01:15.520
One such anomaly is SCP-835.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.079
But before we get started, SCP-835 is an old,
old file.

00:01:20.079 --> 00:01:23.909
It’s one of the earliest in the Foundation’s
database, in fact.

00:01:23.909 --> 00:01:28.789
Like many of the Foundation’s earliest documents,
it’s been heavily redacted and expunged,

00:01:28.789 --> 00:01:31.749
to the point where large blocks of the text
are missing.

00:01:31.749 --> 00:01:35.649
Not to mention the fact that it’s been locked
behind a content filter.

00:01:35.649 --> 00:01:41.249
But SCP-835 is unique not because it’s been
expunged and redacted, but because it’s

00:01:41.249 --> 00:01:43.100
had them lifted.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:48.139
Versions of the file and its addendum that
are cleared of the redactions have been declassified

00:01:48.139 --> 00:01:51.899
and released by order of O5-11 to all viewers.

00:01:51.899 --> 00:01:56.450
For some reason, whatever was so secret about
this file no longer applies.

00:01:56.450 --> 00:02:01.369
But before we take a look at the declassified
documentation, let’s look at the old version

00:02:01.369 --> 00:02:04.560
to get an idea of what exactly we’re dealing
with here.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:09.119
The attached image for SCP-835 is, to put
it simply, gross.

00:02:09.119 --> 00:02:13.739
It’s what appears to be some kind of bone
or muscular growth underwater, a bit like

00:02:13.739 --> 00:02:17.650
coral but much more organic and flesh-like
in shape.

00:02:17.650 --> 00:02:21.510
The growth is mostly white and brown, but
large sections are grown over with what looks

00:02:21.510 --> 00:02:23.920
like some kind of black mold spores.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:30.000
It’s large, too, almost the size of a person’s
chest, and seems to continue out of frame.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:33.660
The caption is simply: “Still image from
Recording 81”.

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:39.849
It’s not even clear if this growth, whatever
it is, is SCP-835 or not.

00:02:39.849 --> 00:02:44.420
Continuing on to the file - the object class
is Keter, and the Special Containment Procedures

00:02:44.420 --> 00:02:47.799
are lengthier than most articles’, and very
detailed.

00:02:47.799 --> 00:02:52.720
They explain that SCP-835 must constantly
be monitored and checked to see if it’s

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.680
growing or expanding.

00:02:54.680 --> 00:02:59.760
In the event that it becomes hostile to Foundation
personnel, something known only as “Suppression

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:05.660
Tactic A-A6” is to be activated until it
ceases any hostile action.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:10.189
The anomaly has to be contained in the open
ocean rather than moved to a water tank or

00:03:10.189 --> 00:03:15.579
such, because of “the highly aggressive
response of SCP-835 to confinement for any

00:03:15.579 --> 00:03:17.069
length of time”.

00:03:17.069 --> 00:03:19.190
So whatever it is, it’s alive.

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:25.249
It’s expanding and growing, and seems capable
of knowing when it’s being placed into containment

00:03:25.249 --> 00:03:26.870
- and responding angrily.

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:30.640
It’s not only sentient, it’s intelligent
and aware.

00:03:30.640 --> 00:03:36.219
They go on to say that SCP-835’s waste has
to be immediately collected and contained,

00:03:36.219 --> 00:03:40.810
and that it is to be fed two times every day,
though what exactly is going to be fed to

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:43.590
it is redacted in this version of the file.

00:03:43.590 --> 00:03:48.430
It can also be moved to a new location up
to two times a year, but only if the current

00:03:48.430 --> 00:03:54.079
location can’t support it anymore, and if
the move has been approved by the site directors.

00:03:54.079 --> 00:04:00.030
On top of that, personnel have to stay away
from SCP-835 - at least fifteen feet.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:03.689
They also need to have safety harnesses attached
to winches on the boat.

00:04:03.689 --> 00:04:09.989
If anyone so much as touches SCP-835, all
of the winches will activate and rapidly yank

00:04:09.989 --> 00:04:11.900
all the divers back to the boat.

00:04:11.900 --> 00:04:16.170
From there, “Suppression Tactic A-A6”
is again instituted.

00:04:16.170 --> 00:04:22.340
But there’s another line: if a staff member
touches SCP-835 and is ‘captured’ by it,

00:04:22.340 --> 00:04:28.110
then the anomaly is to be monitored around
the clock until the subject has been released.

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:30.639
Very ominous containment procedures.

00:04:30.639 --> 00:04:35.950
This predator, if it is a predator, has a
penchant for consuming people and needs to

00:04:35.950 --> 00:04:37.810
be avoided at all costs.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:42.360
But if someone is caught, it… releases them
after a while?

00:04:42.360 --> 00:04:47.699
The description of the document clears some
things up: SCP-835 is a mass of polyps, or

00:04:47.699 --> 00:04:49.830
tissue growths, that resemble coral.

00:04:49.830 --> 00:04:54.710
It’s huge and heavy, though its full weight
is again redacted, and the individual polyps

00:04:54.710 --> 00:05:00.360
are also huge, over a meter long (much longer
than any known coral species).

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:05.990
The central mass is oval and has a huge 3
meter long polyp on each side of it, but can’t

00:05:05.990 --> 00:05:08.090
move or budge because of its huge weight.

00:05:08.090 --> 00:05:12.930
Instead, it uses huge tentacles extending
from the polyps to dig into the ground and

00:05:12.930 --> 00:05:16.180
anchor it in place against the ocean currents.

00:05:16.180 --> 00:05:20.340
These are the same tentacles that are used
for ‘feeding’ and are covered in a sticky

00:05:20.340 --> 00:05:21.699
glue-like adhesive.

00:05:21.699 --> 00:05:26.419
They’re not just long and strong, either
- tests have recorded them damaging stainless

00:05:26.419 --> 00:05:27.960
steel plating.

00:05:27.960 --> 00:05:32.240
And speaking of plating, SCP-835 is covered
in it.

00:05:32.240 --> 00:05:37.050
Not steel, but some kind of organic coral
that’s much harder than steel and couldn’t

00:05:37.050 --> 00:05:39.569
be broken by even diamond-drill bits.

00:05:39.569 --> 00:05:42.169
All the Foundation could get were small samples.

00:05:42.169 --> 00:05:48.860
And if that wasn’t bad enough, the Foundation’s
positive that SCP-835 is growing, like the

00:05:48.860 --> 00:05:54.349
containment procedures suggested, and it's
growing fast, up to fifty pounds in a single

00:05:54.349 --> 00:05:56.720
day if it's left uninterrupted.

00:05:56.720 --> 00:06:01.330
But it can be stopped - it reacts to certain
chemicals that make it “close up” like

00:06:01.330 --> 00:06:05.280
an oyster and stop growing for twenty-four
hours at a time.

00:06:05.280 --> 00:06:09.830
Based on that, the Foundation’s been able
to develop and use a chemical cocktail to

00:06:09.830 --> 00:06:14.370
force it to halt - the aforementioned Suppression
Tactic A-A6.

00:06:14.370 --> 00:06:18.360
However, the results of testing it have been
redacted.

00:06:18.360 --> 00:06:21.980
In case the anomaly wasn’t disgusting enough,
it also vomits.

00:06:21.980 --> 00:06:26.949
That’s right - every couple of hours, it
expels a large mass of some liquidy sludge

00:06:26.949 --> 00:06:30.320
material from both side - so to speak.

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:36.100
After sample testing, the scientists realized
it really is vomit - well, part of it.

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:41.570
The substance is mostly semi-digested food,
fecal material, and semen, but also contains

00:06:41.570 --> 00:06:46.420
live samples of biohazardous viruses, bacteria,
and parasites.

00:06:46.420 --> 00:06:51.050
Some that the Foundation hadn’t even encountered
before SCP-835!

00:06:51.050 --> 00:06:59.090
One of these bacteria, 835-I5 is a big problem
for containing SCP-835, but exactly why that

00:06:59.090 --> 00:07:03.159
is, is unfortunately, expunged from the file
as well.

00:07:03.159 --> 00:07:07.810
Between this lethal witches brew of dangerous
diseases and the diamond-hard shell that covers

00:07:07.810 --> 00:07:14.310
SCP-835’s internal guts, it is nearly impossible
to neutralize or even damage it.

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:18.819
Even if you do crack the shell - the diseased
fluid inside would leak out and infect you

00:07:18.819 --> 00:07:21.229
full of diseases in seconds.

00:07:21.229 --> 00:07:23.780
Wow, that is….kind of crazy.

00:07:23.780 --> 00:07:27.980
Yeah so SCP-835 is a really, really nasty
customer.

00:07:27.980 --> 00:07:33.099
I mean just by looks alone, it’s easy to
tell 835 is probably nothing to mess with.

00:07:33.099 --> 00:07:38.150
But a simple visual of the thing in your line
of sight does no justice in showing how actually

00:07:38.150 --> 00:07:41.030
dangerous and disgusting it really is.

00:07:41.030 --> 00:07:46.129
If you try to break it, you get your immune
system overrun by a cocktail of diseases - if

00:07:46.129 --> 00:07:49.120
it doesn’t manage to eat you first.

00:07:49.120 --> 00:07:55.460
The document has one addendum: an after-action
report by a member of Mobile Task Force Zeta-Nine:

00:07:55.460 --> 00:07:57.610
the notorious “Mole Rats”.

00:07:57.610 --> 00:08:02.310
The Mole Rats are one of the Foundation’s
most elite teams of special operations troops.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:08.189
Like all MTFs, they have a very specific specialization,
one thing they do better than anyone else

00:08:08.189 --> 00:08:09.320
in the world.

00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:12.129
For Zeta-nine, it’s cramped spaces.

00:08:12.129 --> 00:08:17.020
The Task Force is highly-trained in exploring
dangerous constricted areas, especially those

00:08:17.020 --> 00:08:18.820
that lie underground.

00:08:18.820 --> 00:08:23.699
From subterranean caves to endless staircases
and basement labyrinths, the Mole Rats are

00:08:23.699 --> 00:08:27.620
the best of the best at getting in and getting
out.

00:08:27.620 --> 00:08:33.720
The Mobile Task Force Zeta-nine had been performing
an investigation on SCP-835, albeit when it

00:08:33.720 --> 00:08:39.900
was considerably smaller: only a meager four
tons, and hadn’t formed a second big polyp

00:08:39.900 --> 00:08:40.900
yet.

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:44.560
Just like usual, four members of the Mole
Rats were chosen to begin the investigation,

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:49.480
equipped with underwater isolation suits to
ward off any biological threats.

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:55.100
Lieutenant C , Sergeants L and M, and Corporal
H, a rookie team member who was training with

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:56.950
them and was ordered to only observe.

00:08:56.950 --> 00:09:01.640
They took a small underwater drone with them
- one that would come in very handy.

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:06.980
At first, SCP-835 didn’t act hostile or
aggressive towards the members of the team.

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:11.270
In fact, it even allowed members to swim up
to it and touch it without reacting.

00:09:11.270 --> 00:09:15.899
They couldn’t even tell if it was alive
or not, so they sent the drone to approach

00:09:15.899 --> 00:09:20.410
the huge polyp on the north side while they
went around to the small entrance on the other

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:21.959
side of the rock.

00:09:21.959 --> 00:09:26.089
Corporal H was told to remain there and make
sure that the power cable to the drone didn’t

00:09:26.089 --> 00:09:27.470
break off or snap.

00:09:27.470 --> 00:09:29.760
Everything seemed calm.

00:09:29.760 --> 00:09:33.590
Suddenly the drone’s claw arm jerked back,
having gotten stuck in something, and began

00:09:33.590 --> 00:09:35.100
thrashing around.

00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:38.779
Not wanting to wake the creature, Corporal
H moved forward and tried to free the claw

00:09:38.779 --> 00:09:41.010
- but then he became trapped too.

00:09:41.010 --> 00:09:45.060
The other members of the team heard him on
the radio, screaming for them to come and

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:49.230
help him, and that he’d been grabbed by
some “horrible tentacle thing” that was

00:09:49.230 --> 00:09:53.930
dragging him towards the polyp, that had opened
up into a mouth.

00:09:53.930 --> 00:09:56.560
The incident left Lieutenant C a bit ruffled
afterward:

00:09:56.560 --> 00:09:57.560
“Jesus Christ.

00:09:57.560 --> 00:09:59.110
I can’t do this, he was just a kid!

00:09:59.110 --> 00:10:01.649
It was his first mission, I should’ve kept
my eye on him!”.

00:10:01.649 --> 00:10:05.540
After a moment, she composes herself, and
begins to explain what happened:

00:10:05.540 --> 00:10:08.940
“The anomaly grabbed Corporal H, having
fooled the rest of us.

00:10:08.940 --> 00:10:13.050
What we thought was the entrance was just
some cave, while the polyp on the north side

00:10:13.050 --> 00:10:16.620
was the real “entrance” into SCP-835.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:20.980
The tentacles came out of it’s smaller polyps,
grabbed Corporal H and began dragging him

00:10:20.980 --> 00:10:23.380
in while he thrashed around and screamed.

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:28.440
The boat tried to pull in the winch, but from
all the activity, the line snapped in two.

00:10:28.440 --> 00:10:32.480
Corporal H was pulled inside SCP-835 and eaten”.

00:10:32.480 --> 00:10:36.880
The Lieutenant explains that she swam over
and hooked herself to his outreached hand

00:10:36.880 --> 00:10:38.790
when the boat began winching her up.

00:10:38.790 --> 00:10:42.650
She said just as she assured him that they’re
going to be fine and that she’s not letting

00:10:42.650 --> 00:10:46.730
go, her line snapped and they were both suddenly
pulled inside.

00:10:46.730 --> 00:10:51.701
She breaks for a moment, before describing
the inside as like a wet, pulsing tube, like

00:10:51.701 --> 00:10:54.360
how intestines look on colonoscopies.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:58.730
They were both steadily being pulled in by
the muscle contractions - what doctors call

00:10:58.730 --> 00:11:04.470
peristalsis, the way your body moves food
down your throat and through your intestines.

00:11:04.470 --> 00:11:08.690
The only reason they weren’t dissolved or
crushed was because of the isolation suits

00:11:08.690 --> 00:11:11.950
they were wearing, but they still couldn’t
move.

00:11:11.950 --> 00:11:15.670
Corporal H had vomited in his suit, but they
were both alive.

00:11:15.670 --> 00:11:19.170
The Lieutenant, thinking fast, figured out
that if they were moving through its body,

00:11:19.170 --> 00:11:22.610
they would come out the other end in seventy
two hours.

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:27.510
They had air and water in the suits, but little
battery - and if the heat went out, they would

00:11:27.510 --> 00:11:29.090
freeze to death.

00:11:29.090 --> 00:11:33.500
She quickly killed all of the lights and power
in both their suits to the minimum - except

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:37.490
the helmet lights, so they could make sure
the other was still alive.

00:11:37.490 --> 00:11:41.810
The pair stayed like that for a whole day,
with absolutely nothing but the creature’s

00:11:41.810 --> 00:11:44.040
digestion and their own breathing.

00:11:44.040 --> 00:11:48.410
After a while, the Corporal’s face was visible
- he looked tired and scared.

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:51.840
She says that thirteen hours in, the kid started
talking and babbling.

00:11:51.840 --> 00:11:56.000
She calmed him down and they both slept for
a bit, but were rudely awoken by falling into

00:11:56.000 --> 00:11:57.660
the stomach of the creature.

00:11:57.660 --> 00:12:02.611
They both fell out into a small chamber filled
with liquid - and barely a moment later, their

00:12:02.611 --> 00:12:05.570
suits began to melt in the stomach acid.

00:12:05.570 --> 00:12:10.639
She yelled and they both ran for a hole in
the wall - SCP-835’s sphincter.

00:12:10.639 --> 00:12:14.959
At this point it was very clear that they
made it into the intestine - and it was worse

00:12:14.959 --> 00:12:15.959
than the stomach.

00:12:15.959 --> 00:12:19.970
I’m sure you can imagine how horrifying
it must have been to be in the mix of this

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:21.690
creature’s fecal waste.

00:12:21.690 --> 00:12:25.670
Disgusted and vomiting, the Corporal and Lieutenant
picked each other up, knowing they were making

00:12:25.670 --> 00:12:28.029
strides of the terrible ordeal.

00:12:28.029 --> 00:12:34.310
But reached a dead stop - the creatures rectal
hole was tightly shut, blocking their escape.

00:12:34.310 --> 00:12:39.120
They decided to wait, knowing it would have
to excrete eventually - and after an undetermined

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:43.170
amount of time - I mean any time spent in
some thing’s intestines waiting to be pooped

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:48.990
out is too much time - The Lieutenant was
shot out into the sea - but without the Corporal.

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:54.399
She is obviously angry, telling the agents
to do something “expunged” before declaring

00:12:54.399 --> 00:12:56.380
she needs a drink and to sleep.

00:12:56.380 --> 00:13:00.279
What a horrifying story - but there are gaps.

00:13:00.279 --> 00:13:03.810
Let’s take a look at the uncensored documentation
for SCP-835.

00:13:03.810 --> 00:13:07.149
First, let’s go back to the containment
procedures.

00:13:07.149 --> 00:13:13.510
What SCP-835 is to be fed is explained: any
kind of local fish, but higher level mammals

00:13:13.510 --> 00:13:17.149
if it goes into a “rage state” - including
humans.

00:13:17.149 --> 00:13:21.769
In fact, it seems to calm down when digesting
higher mammals - maybe it’s developed a

00:13:21.769 --> 00:13:23.330
taste for human flesh.

00:13:23.330 --> 00:13:27.269
In any case, the feedings should never happen
without heavy supervision.

00:13:27.269 --> 00:13:32.300
Next, the results of performing tests on the
samples of SCP-835 the Foundation was able

00:13:32.300 --> 00:13:33.300
to get.

00:13:33.300 --> 00:13:39.860
SCP-835 is no normal coral: it seems to be
made from what can only be described as “basic

00:13:39.860 --> 00:13:41.839
human biological components”.

00:13:41.839 --> 00:13:47.339
The hard outer shell is super-dense calcium,
like your bones but hundreds of times harder.

00:13:47.339 --> 00:13:51.630
The polyps are covered with the same kind
of enamel that you’d find on your teeth,

00:13:51.630 --> 00:13:56.630
and the fleshy muscle that the tentacles are
made of is mostly mutated tongue cells.

00:13:56.630 --> 00:14:01.389
The creature seems to have most of the biological
systems we have, but they’ve all degraded

00:14:01.389 --> 00:14:08.160
or mutated into almost unrecognizability - except
the digestive and reproductive systems, which

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:10.380
are highly advanced.

00:14:10.380 --> 00:14:18.160
835-I5, the bacteria unique to the anomaly,
is explained: it’s how SCP-835 reproduces.

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:22.560
When vertebrates are infected with it, they
will undergo a variety of symptoms, gaining

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:26.610
huge amounts of weight despite always being
hungry for things that normally can’t be

00:14:26.610 --> 00:14:29.399
eaten like wood and raw meat.

00:14:29.399 --> 00:14:33.259
Their skin will harden and form polyps across
its surface.

00:14:33.259 --> 00:14:37.490
Their biological systems will slowly stop
working, and they’ll become aggressive.

00:14:37.490 --> 00:14:42.860
And then, they will drastically reduce in
intelligence and motion except for the desire

00:14:42.860 --> 00:14:44.459
to enter the sea.

00:14:44.459 --> 00:14:45.600
Sound familiar?

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:52.310
That’s right: being infected by it turns
the victim into another SCP-835 instance,

00:14:52.310 --> 00:14:54.209
with no way to cure it.

00:14:54.209 --> 00:15:01.590
And just like it seems, SCP-835 is still somewhat
aware and intelligent - at one point, this

00:15:01.590 --> 00:15:04.000
thing was a normal human.

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:08.529
Just in case that’s not horrible enough,
the after-action report has also been thoroughly

00:15:08.529 --> 00:15:09.529
declassified.

00:15:09.529 --> 00:15:13.370
Let’s take another look to see the real,
full story of what happened to Lieutenant

00:15:13.370 --> 00:15:17.560
C and Corporal H inside SCP-835.

00:15:17.560 --> 00:15:21.029
The first reveal is when Corporal H was being
pulled into the polyp.

00:15:21.029 --> 00:15:25.810
He was screaming and crying, begging for help:
“Oh God, it’s eating me, I don’t want

00:15:25.810 --> 00:15:26.810
to die!”.

00:15:26.810 --> 00:15:31.840
Command tells Lieutenant C to abort the mission,
but she refuses to leave one of her men behind,

00:15:31.840 --> 00:15:33.910
holding his hand while hooking them together.

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:37.290
Then the line snapped and they were pulled
in.

00:15:37.290 --> 00:15:41.819
Just as they were escaping the stomach and
right as she hit the sphincter, she realized

00:15:41.819 --> 00:15:47.120
- the walls of the stomach were lined with
human faces, screaming and wailing and begging

00:15:47.120 --> 00:15:48.440
to be killed.

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:52.740
She pulled her weapon out and began firing
into them, and she would’ve melted if Corporal

00:15:52.740 --> 00:15:54.650
H hadn’t pushed her through.

00:15:54.650 --> 00:15:59.470
In the intestine, the Corporal began to complain
of a rancid smell - she checked, and realized

00:15:59.470 --> 00:16:02.240
he had a breach in his suit, but quickly patched
it.

00:16:02.240 --> 00:16:06.980
But it was too late - she looked at his face,
and it was growing pustules already.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:10.720
They burst, spraying blood, and he begged
to be put out of his misery.

00:16:10.720 --> 00:16:15.279
But when the Lieutenant shot her gun at him,
all it produced were empty clicks.

00:16:15.279 --> 00:16:19.530
She had wasted all the ammo on the crying
stomach faces.

00:16:19.530 --> 00:16:23.760
Suddenly tentacles burst through the Corporals
faceplate and simultaneously pinned the Lieutenant

00:16:23.760 --> 00:16:24.760
down.

00:16:24.760 --> 00:16:28.529
She managed to flip what had been the Corporal
over and wrestle what was left of him back

00:16:28.529 --> 00:16:32.970
through the sphincter into the stomach, where
his body began to melt in the acid.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:38.410
But before it did, she saw the Corporal’s
face, smiling, and saying he loved her before

00:16:38.410 --> 00:16:39.550
he died.

00:16:39.550 --> 00:16:42.399
Then she felt a burst of energy and was shot
through the exit.

00:16:42.399 --> 00:16:46.899
With a troubled gleem in her eye she stands
there telling her story to the agnet.

00:16:46.899 --> 00:16:51.550
She takes a second to gain some strength and
then says “I didn’t make it out intact.

00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:55.519
My suit was breached, and I didn’t even
realize until I took it off and saw the rash

00:16:55.519 --> 00:16:56.610
on my skin.”

00:16:56.610 --> 00:17:01.560
Realizing she’s going to die, she suddenly
puts the room she’s in on lockdown and orders

00:17:01.560 --> 00:17:05.780
the debriefing agent to evacuate everyone
else aboard immediately.

00:17:05.780 --> 00:17:10.580
Just before she kills the feed, she makes
one request: that the Foundation not try to

00:17:10.580 --> 00:17:12.900
decontaminate the small boat.

00:17:12.900 --> 00:17:19.330
Just to abandon ship and scuttle it on top
of SCP-835, on top of the Corporal.

00:17:19.330 --> 00:17:23.910
That way, they can be together, in some kind
of sick resting place.

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:29.580
SCP-835 is the horrible tale of things that
can go wrong at the Foundation and two people

00:17:29.580 --> 00:17:32.260
doing their best in a brutal situation.

00:17:32.260 --> 00:17:36.860
But with the modern containment protocols
and ensuring people know what happened to

00:17:36.860 --> 00:17:41.700
the pair, the Foundation can ensure no one
ends up like the Lieutenant and the Corporal

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:42.700
again.

00:17:42.700 --> 00:17:49.720
Now go watch “SCP-3000 - Anantashesha”
and “SCP-057-IT - Under the Sea” for more

00:17:49.720 --> 00:17:54.510
SCP Explained videos about mysterious anomalies
that can be found lurking beneath the waves.

00:17:54.510 --> 00:17:55.440
Surf’s up!

